#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# differential_root

#% text
# `differential_root(f)` stands for the function defined by `f(y, x)`: a list of a linear ordinary differential equation for y(x) and its initial values at one point. `differential_root(f)(x0)` gives its value at an inexact real x0.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The value is computed by `n_dsolve_value` from the initial point to x0. Exact arguments leave the call as it is.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
differential_root((y, x) => [y'(x) - y(x) == 0, y(0) == 1])(0.5)
#% output
#= 1.6487212707001309

#% cell
differential_root((y, x) => [y''(x) + y(x) == 0, y(0) == 0, y'(0) == 1])(1.0)
#% output
#= 0.8414709848078933

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `difference_root`, `n_dsolve_value`, `d_solve`
